{"id":"atsresume","name":"atsresume","aliases":[],"caption":"A one-column resume class with PDF text that applicant tracking systems can","authors":[{"id":"superlede","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Super Lede","year":"2026"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"1.0.0","date":""},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n     atsresume is a LaTeX class for a one-page resume. The layout is a single\n     column: the name centered at the top, section headings in capitals over a thin\n     rule, and places and dates on the right margin.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n     The class keeps the PDF text complete and in reading order for applicant\n     tracking systems (ATS) and other resume parsers; how well a given system fills\n     in its fields still depends on that system. Places and dates are pushed to the\n     margin with glue instead of a table or a second column, ligatures and\n     hyphenation are turned off, bullets are the Unicode bullet character, and a\n     heading never ends a page.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n     It works with pdfLaTeX, LuaLaTeX and XeLaTeX, on US Letter and A4, and needs\n     only packages from TeX Live's small scheme. The text is set in TeX Gyre\n     Pagella.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/atsresume/README.md"},{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/atsresume/atsresume-doc.pdf"}],"home":"https://readableresume.com","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/atsresume","file":true},"texlive":"atsresume","topics":["class","cv"]}